; win32.def -- Windows API -> DLL ownership table (single source of truth).
;
; Parsed at goc build time by loadWin32Def (codegen.go) into the externDLL
; map used by Gen to emit "extern Name, dll" imports. Adding a Windows API is
; therefore a one-line data change here -- no Go source edit, no recompile.
;
; Syntax:
;   ; comment / blank line      ignored
;   # <dll>                     start a group; following bare lines belong
;                               to this DLL (no ".dll" suffix needed)
;   <FunctionName>              an exported function of the current group
;
; Keep the per-group lists alphabetised. Function names must also exist in
; the windows.h family of headers (prototypes) and, when used inside
; goclib.asm, in that block's "; @extern" line -- the def only answers
; "which DLL".

